# 1. CORE CONCEPT

AETHER is a personal music playground.

Users can load audio files stored locally on their computers, play their music, and experience beautiful real-time visualizations that react to the actual audio signal.

While listening, users can switch between visualizers, play with ambient environments, use a minimal productivity tool, draw, experiment with generative art, explore a little interactive toy, or simply relax and watch the music.

The music must continue playing while users navigate between supported experiences inside the application.

This should feel like a place people open when they want to listen to music, focus, relax, explore, or escape into their own digital atmosphere.

The website must not require a paid API, a backend, a database, a login, or an external music streaming service for its core functionality.

All uploaded music should be processed locally in the browser. Never upload a user's audio files to a server.

